# VM profile: ONE 2 vCPU / 8 GiB VM that is master, worker, Kafka broker, NFS server and driver host at once
# (spark-master alone, before spark-w1 / spark-w2 exist). Use with SPARK_WORKER_HOSTS=(spark-master) in cluster.env.
# Every Spark setting is the same as in a real cluster (spark-submit to spark://spark-master:7077, shared checkpoints),
# only smaller, so everything fits on one VM next to the broker:
#
#   1 Kafka container 1024 + master daemon 512 + driver 1024 + driver overhead 384
#   + 1 executor x (1536 + 1024 overhead) + worker daemon 512 + 1 OS reserve 1024              = 7040 MB of 8192
# lib.sh adds the worker side to the master total when the master is also a worker. The ~1 GB left over (the kernel
# reports ~7.75 GB) is for the replay producer and the soak sampler, which run on the same VM.
# Executors: 1 (2 cores / 2 cores per executor). With 2 vCPUs, Kafka, the driver and the producer share the same cores,
# so throughput numbers from this layout are a lower bound, not a scaling result.

: "${VM_MEMORY:=8g}"
: "${OS_RESERVE_MB:=1024}"
: "${DRIVER_OVERHEAD_MB:=384}"

: "${KAFKA_HEAP:=512m}"                   # what the earlier standalone container on this VM ran with
: "${KAFKA_CONTAINER_MEMORY:=1024m}"

: "${SPARK_WORKER_CORES:=2}"
: "${SPARK_WORKER_MEMORY:=1536m}"
: "${SPARK_EXECUTOR_CORES:=2}"
: "${SPARK_EXECUTOR_MEMORY:=1536m}"
: "${SPARK_EXECUTOR_MEMORY_OVERHEAD:=1024m}"
: "${SPARK_DAEMON_MEMORY:=512m}"

: "${SPARK_DRIVER_MEMORY:=1g}"
